# Reproducible analysis reports generated by `python3 -m src.run_analysis`
# (regenerated from source data; version a specific snapshot deliberately
# if the team ever wants to, rather than committing every run's output).
reports/generated/

# Scratch, executed copies of a notebook produced while verifying it runs
# end to end (e.g. via `jupytext --execute` / `nbconvert --execute --output
# *.executed.ipynb`). The paired source notebooks (notebooks/0_starter_eda.ipynb,
# 1_full_dataset_eda.ipynb, 2_full_dataset_modeling.ipynb) are intentionally
# committed and are NOT matched by this pattern.
*.executed.ipynb

# Kaggle kernel push copies (scripts/push_kaggle_kernel.sh): each
# notebooks/kernels/<slug>/kernel-metadata.json is committed, but the
# .ipynb the script copies alongside it every push is not - it's always a
# fresh copy of the real source in notebooks/, so committing it would just
# be a second, easily-stale version to keep in sync by hand.
notebooks/kernels/*/*.ipynb

# Large competition datasets (exclude big data files)
data/**/*.csv
data/**/*.pkl
data/**/*.xlsx
data/**/*.zip
data/**/*.json
data/**/*.h5
data/**/*.parquet
!data/README.md

